There are 34 positive integers n ≤ 20000 for which the number of isomorphism types of groups of order n has been determined but a complete, explicit list of representative groups (one for each isomorphism type) is not available. These orders are:

(i) n = 2^10 = 1024;
(ii) the 32 orders of the following forms:
   • 2^9 · p, where p is an odd prime with 2^9 · p ≤ 20000;
   • 2^8 · p · q, where p ∈ {3, 5, 7} and q is a prime with q ∉ {2, p} and 2^8 · p · q ≤ 20000;
   • 2^7 · 3^2 · p, where p is a prime with p ∉ {2, 3} and 2^7 · 3^2 · p ≤ 20000;
   • the specific orders 8640, 9600, 13440, 16320, 17280, 19440;
(iii) n = 12500.

For each such order n, explicitly construct a complete and irredundant list of finite groups of order n, that is, exhibit (e.g. via presentations, polycyclic generating sequences, or some other explicit description) one representative from every isomorphism class of groups of order n.

